Email corpus for the document renderer (D32), rendered by test/doc/email.zig
against test/golden/doc/email-*.png. Written for this corpus to mimic the
HTML that common senders and clients produce (a store's receipt, a
Mailchimp-style newsletter, Gmail, Outlook, and Apple Mail replies); the
names, addresses, and text are invented.

schemes/ holds mail for the color scheme tests in test/abi/docview.zig
(D32): an Outlook mobile reply, a notification with a logo for light
backgrounds (cid/), a newsletter with a colored band and buttons, a bare
Gmail-style mail and plain text made into HTML (no colors), and a mail
with its own prefers-color-scheme: dark styles. Invented as well.
